<header class="tool-page-header container">
  <a class="back-link" href="../index.html">← All tools</a>
  <p class="eyebrow">MAC · Vendor lookup</p>
  <h1>MAC address lookup.</h1>
  <p>Enter a MAC address or its first six hexadecimal characters to identify the registered hardware vendor.</p>
</header>
<section class="tool-workspace container" data-mac-tool data-api-endpoint="https://the-tech-shed-mac-lookup.will-4c9.workers.dev/lookup">
  <form class="tool-panel" data-mac-form novalidate>
    <div class="field-group">
      <label for="mac-address">MAC address or OUI</label>
      <input id="mac-address" name="mac" type="text" inputmode="text" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="characters" spellcheck="false" value="44:38:39:FF:EF:57" placeholder="44:38:39:FF:EF:57" aria-describedby="mac-hint mac-error">
      <p class="field-hint" id="mac-hint">Colons, hyphens, dots and plain hexadecimal formats are accepted. You can also enter a six-character OUI such as <code>443839</code>.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="privacy-note"><strong>Privacy note:</strong> The normalised address is sent to The Tech Shed’s lookup service and then to the MACVendors API. Nothing is stored by this page.</p>
    <p class="form-error" id="mac-error" data-mac-error role="alert" hidden></p>
    <button class="button" type="submit" data-mac-submit>Look up vendor</button>
  </form>
  <div class="tool-results mac-results" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
    <div class="results-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Lookup result</p><h2 data-mac-vendor>Ready to search</h2></div></div>
    <dl class="result-grid">
      <div><dt>Address</dt><dd data-mac-address>—</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Status</dt><dd data-mac-status>Waiting</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p class="result-note" data-mac-note>Enter an address to query the registered vendor database.</p>
    <p class="result-attribution">Vendor data provided by <a href="https://macvendors.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">MACVendors</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>
